# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — session realm isolation.
#
# Each session gets its own realm, so a top-level `var` is a slot on
# THAT realm's globals and not on the shared Global namespace.  This
# fixture pins the single-session half; that the var is invisible to
# another session is in two_session_isolation.chk.

# Set a realm-local var (Realm.x is per-session by construction).

## mode: repl
> {"id":4,"op":"eval","code":"var localcell = 7; localcell"}
< "id":4 | "kind":"result" | "value":"7"
< "id":4 | "kind":"done"

# Confirm it's NOT visible on Global (Global is a VM singleton).
# Accessing an undefined slot raises a runtime error.
> {"id":5,"op":"eval","code":"Global.localcell"}
< "id":5 | "kind":"error"
< "id":5 | "kind":"done"
